<programme start="20261110210000 +0000" stop="20261110230000 +0000" channel="FS2 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Basketball</title><sub-title lang="en">Illinois State at Purdue</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Illinois State Redbirds visit the Purdue Boilermakers for an NCAA Division I game. Illinois State comes off a 100-55 victory over Central State alongside guard Johnny Kinziger, and Purdue rides a two-game skid with forward Daniel Jacobsen.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Basketball</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191260_b_v8_az.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261110230000 +0000" stop="20261111020000 +0000" channel="FS2 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Cincinnati at Houston</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 17 Cougars meet the Bearcats at TDECU Stadium for a Big 12 game. Houston leans on nine third-down conversions from a 6-2 start, while 5-3 Cincinnati counts on three team sacks and two takeaways from an Oct. 31 game to secure a Big 12 victory.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261111020000 +0000" stop="20261111030000 +0000" channel="FS2 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Nebraska at Illinois</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Nebraska Cornhuskers (5-3) visit the Illinois Fighting Illini (5-3) at Gies Memorial Stadium. Nebraska seeks to snap a three-game skid after falling 17-10 to Washington and relies on Anthony Colandrea who has 15 TDs. Illinois beat Maryland 20-17.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261111030000 +0000" stop="20261111040000 +0000" channel="FS2 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">UCLA at Minnesota</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 8 UCLA Bruins (8-0) face the Minnesota Golden Gophers (5-3) at Huntington Bank Stadium for a Big Ten game. UCLA enters undefeated in eight games after shutting out Nevada 27-0, while Minnesota is coming off a 23-16 overtime defeat to Indiana.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
